<title>GERMANY: Oil World sees lower 96/97 world rapeseed supply.</title>
<headline>Oil World sees lower 96/97 world rapeseed supply.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>World rapeseed and canola production is forecast at 30.05 million tonnes in 1996/97, down 13 percent from 1995/96, the Oil World newsletter said.</p>
<p>The independent publication cited area reductions in Canada, Europe, China and Australia and crop losses in Eastern Europe, Germany and Scandinavia.</p>
<p>Eastern Europe would turn from a net exporter of about 600,000 tonnes last season into a net importer of 100,000 in July/June 1996/97, mostly from the EU, Oil World said.</p>
<p>EU exports would rise to 300,000 tonnes from 120,000 last season, while imports would fall by 25 percent to 250,000.  </p>
<p>High prices as a result of supply tightness had forced crushers to cut rape processing in August and September and this decline in output would continue.</p>
<p>EU crushings were forecast at 6.55 million tonnes in 1996/97 versus 8.05 million in 1995/96. Oil stocks remained comfortable, but low meal stocks meant there was no reserve.</p>
<p>-Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
